MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_001: Alright, I think this should be enough.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_002: Huh? What's up with all the little rocks, Cai?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_003: They're part of a training method my dad taught me.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_004: Toss all the rocks into the air, then dodge them as\nthey fall back down.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_005: Th-there's no way! No one can do that! There's\ntoo many!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_006: Wrong! Just watch. You'll see. Hyah!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_007: WHAAAA?! Look ou— Huh?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_008: Hyah-huh-hyah!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_009: Amazing. Not even one of them hit you.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_010: So you just do this over and over. Doesn't cost\nanything either. Pretty neat, eh?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_011: Over and over... Even though it'd hurt if you got hit.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_012: It's fine! The secret is just don't get hit. And after a\nfew tries, you learn to see where the rocks are going.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_013: And even if you do get hit, they're just small rocks.\nThink about how much worse a blade would feel.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_014: OK... I guess when you put it that way, I sort of have\nto agree.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_015: Right! And if you master this lesson, you'll learn to\ndodge your enemy's attacks. 
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_016: I see... Well, maybe I should try it, then.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_017: Yes, you should! And here we go!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_018: Ow ow ow ow! I can't dodge all this! No way!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_019: Whoa... Peter, you alright?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_020: Ugh. I know they're small, but they still sting!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_021: Haha. Let's try a different lesson.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_022: Sounds good, I think. Wait... What kind of lesson?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_023: Running with armor. I put some over there.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_024: Isn't that armor meant for adults? It's bigger than\nwe are.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_025: It's not a problem. Let's go!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_026: If Cai can do it, I can do it.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_027: Haaah... Haaah... Ughhh...
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_028: Whoa... Peter, are you alright?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_029: That's exactly what you said after the last test! I can't\nrun with something so heavy on my back!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_030: I think you're gonna have to train in a way that\nworks for you, Peter.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_031: Are you saying I can't keep up with you, Cai?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_032: I've been training like this since I was little.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_033: I'm used to the stones and the armor. But maybe you\nneed to start with something less challenging.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_034: Ohh... But I'm a little older than you!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_035: Does that even matter?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_C_036: It does! I swear I'll make it work for me, somehow!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_001: There... I think this will be enough.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_002: Peter, why'd you call me out here. What's with all\nthe little rocks?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_003: They're for training, obviously. Watch this. Hyup!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_004: Nice! That was great! Not a single rock hit you!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_005: Yeah, pretty good, eh? This way of doing the rock\ntest is perfect for me, don't you think?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_006: This way of doing... Oh, yeah, I get it. You're putting\nyour amazing eyesight to good use, huh?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_007: You watch closely, and you can see the rocks' paths.\nLast time, you got scared and looked away.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_008: Yeah, I can read the rocks pretty well now, but not\nas well as you can.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_009: That's still amazing! I had to go through a lot of pain\nand effort to master this lesson.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_010: And I had a lot of help from my dad. You did this all\non your own, Peter. That's incredible.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_011: Hehe. It is, isn't it? Feel free to praise me as much\nas you want.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_012: I think we're ready for the next level. Pop taught me\nlots of training methods.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_013: Uhh...
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_014: Another training partner is just what I need. You're\nup for anything, right, Peter?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_015: Now hold on a sec... "Anything" might be a bit much,\ndon't you think?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_016: I mean, I just got the hang of the rock thing.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_017: And that's because I slowly added a few rocks at a\ntime. The running-with-armor test... There's no way.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_018: This is gonna be great! We'll train so hard! We'll be\nevenly matched in no time!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_019: We've known each other since we were babies!\nOf course we'll be awesome training partners!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_020: Uh... Wh-when you put it like that...
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_021: Oh, fine. I'll train with you, Cai. I can do anythi—\nI can do anything!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_022: Yes! This will be so much fun! Now, where should\nwe start?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_023: We'll have to build our muscles with some basic\ndrills. But we need some combat training too...
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_024: Like Pop says, "Train to beat up an atlas bear with\nyour bare hands, and everything will fall into place."
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_025: Aw, Pop... I hope I'm as strong as you someday.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_B_026: Train to fight a bear?! Your dad's a vulkan! Don't\nyou think we should start a little slower?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_001: Haaah... Haaah... *cough*
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_002: Peter! Stand up straight! Time for some bare-\nknuckle fighting!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_003: H-hold on... We already ran around with heavy\narmor tied to our backs.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_004: And you had us carry pails of water too.\nWhat's the point?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_005: You can't stop now! We're simulating the extreme\nexhaustion of an all-out battle!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_006: What more do you want? I've got the "extreme\nexhaustion" part down. I can't even stand anymore.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_007: Stop arguing with your trainer! Ngh... Ah!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_008: What now, Cai? I need to rest!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_009: No! Peter! Behind you!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_010: MWRRROOOAAARRRRRR!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_011: Aaaaaah! Atlas bear!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_012: Watch out, Peter! Agh...
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_013: Cai! Don't be stupid! You don't even have a weapon!\nWe need to run!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_014: No! I can take this thing!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_015: GHHHWROAR!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_016: {SetColor=Gray}It didn't even flinch! But I have to buy Peter some\ntime to escape!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_017: No! Big mistake, Cai! You can't stay here! I'm not\nletting you!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_018: Whaaa?! Peter?! What are you doing?! Put me down!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_019: You never listen! So I'm getting us out of this!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_020: Stop! You can't carry me up the cliff! Put me down!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_021: This is our only chance! It's the only way we can\nget out of this togeth— Aughhh!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_022: ROOOAR! GRKH...
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_023: Owowow... Wh-what? We knocked out the bear!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_024: I can't believe we landed right on top of it. That's\npure luck right there.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_025: Well, the move we just did was basically a classic\nDouble Brother Brutal Bear Bounce.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_026: Yeah, and actually, you did land a hit on it. So I\nguess we won this fight?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_027: We won because of you, Peter. When did you get\nstrong enough to carry me?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_028: I'm as shocked as you are. All our training paid off!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_029: What a way to take out an atlas bear! And with our\n"bare hands," just like Pop said!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_030: I don't know if we technically beat up this bear, like\nCastor said, but that was pretty amazing.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_031: When we fight together, we can "beat up" anything!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_032: That's right! The two of us will always... Huh.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_033: What's wrong, Peter?
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_034: You'll live a lot longer than me, won't you, Cai?\nBut at least we'll be together after we die.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_035: And you're right. We can win any fight, together.
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_036: Yep... Exactly!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_037: With my best bro around, nothing's gonna get me!
MID_SE_Kai_Pet_A_038: Hehe. I have to knock out a bear for you to call me\nyour "best bro," eh? You know what? I'll take it.